package form

// Desc describes the form control to the agent, for Library.Control.
const Desc = "Form the user fills and submits. A submit gives {\"data\": object, \"submit\": string}, data holding each filled field's value by name. Every rule in params, field types and validate functions included, is enforced before a submit reaches you, unless its button has novalidate, and the user sees each broken rule's error message: don't re-check what those rules cover, in submitted data or in values you prefill. A field with min 1 and max 1 holds exactly one item, read [0]; where rules are enforced, only optional fields can be missing. The form keeps what the user entered, after a submit and when it is shown again, such as after its slot is set: to have the user fix something only the script can check, show why and call ui.draw() again. In a row, it fills the space left on its line."
